            "slot": "s64",
            "repere": "Intertitre · Johns Hopkins Medicine recently report…",
            "text": "Johns Hopkins Medicine recently reported that, according to the Dietary Guidelines for Americans, “it’s safe for most people to drink three to five cups of coffee a day with a maximum intake of 400 milligrams of caffeine.” (<span style=\"color:rgb(62, 120, 189)\">source</span>)<br><br>They reported multiple benefits of drinking coffee, including the following:",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s66",
            "repere": "Point · Coffee drinkers are less likely to die…",
            "text": "Coffee drinkers are less likely to die from some of the leading causes of death.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s67",
            "repere": "Point · Coffee...contains antioxidants and oth…",
            "text": "Coffee...contains antioxidants and other active substances that may reduce internal inflammation and protect against disease.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s68",
            "repere": "Point · Dark roast coffee decreases breakage i…",
            "text": "Dark roast coffee decreases breakage in DNA strands, which occur naturally but can lead to cancer or tumors if not repaired by your cells.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s69",
            "repere": "Point · ...coffee drinkers - decaf or regular …",
            "text": "...coffee drinkers - decaf or regular - were 26 percent less likely to develop colorectal cancer.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s70",
            "repere": "Point · Coffee is chock-full of substances tha…",
            "text": "Coffee is chock-full of substances that may help guard against...Alzheimer's disease and heart disease.",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s72",
            "repere": "Intertitre · With all these benefits, however, ther…",
            "text": "With all these benefits, however, there’s a big risk in drinking coffee: pesticides, mycotoxins, and molds.<br><br>One research study found that 91.7% of the coffee samples they tested contained molds. (<span style=\"color:rgb(62, 120, 189)\">source</span>)<br><br>So what do you do?",
            "image": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "element",
          "settings": {
            "slot": "s73",
            "repere": "Intertitre · It was to that coffee that I’ve compar…",
            "text": "<br>It was to that coffee that I’ve compared everything else.<br><br>This coffee is clean, healthy, non-GMO, and as pure as you can get with just one simple ingredient:",
